# --- COMMIT CONVENTIONS (@vicacha-devs/medusa-v2-extensions) ---
# Allowed <type> values:
#   feat     - New plugin capability, Medusa v2 module, workflow, admin route, or API endpoint
#   fix      - Bug fix in admin UI, workflows, providers, or API routes
#   docs     - Documentation and README updates
#   style    - Code formatting or Admin UI styling adjustments
#   refactor - Refactoring code (e.g., splitting files to stay <= 500 lines)
#   perf     - Query, indexing, caching, or bundle performance improvements
#   test     - Adding or updating node --test or Playwright E2E tests
#   build    - Plugin build, Turborepo, or dependency updates
#   ci       - GitHub Actions, Changesets, or monorepo QA scripts
#   chore    - Routine maintenance tasks
#   revert   - Revert a previous commit
#
# Allowed <scope> values (package/plugin name):
#   b2b, barcode, dian, documents, fulfillment-eu, notifications, odoo,
#   payment-bold, payment-mollie, product-extensions, social-commerce,
#   stories, typesense, shared, plugin-testing, sandbox, docs,
#   eslint-config, typescript-config, repo, deps
#
# Examples:
#   feat(b2b): add approval threshold workflow for company quotes
#   fix(payment-bold): handle constant-time HMAC verification on webhook replay
